(7)
"blank cartridge" means a cartridge without a bullet or any other projectile;
(8)
"blank firing firearms" means firearms capable of firing a blank cartridge;
(9)
"bullet" means the conical head of the cartridge normally made of lead or copper that is expelled out of barrel or cylinder
by means of explosive charge or compressed air or other gas;
(10)
"caliber" means the internal diameter or bore of the barrel of a firearm measured in inches or millimeters or geometric
circumference;
(11)
"carry" means to bear a small arm, upon, about or in the proximity of one's person;
(12)
"cartridge" means a complete object consisting of a cartridge case, primer, propellant, bullet or any single or multiple
projectile;

